<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Biocel Q1 net loss widens by 8 pct.</title>
<headline>Czech Biocel Q1 net loss widens by 8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Biocel Paskov a.s. for three months ending March 31, 1997, according to Czech accounting standards</p>
<p>(in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> Net result		  144.72 loss vs	   133.12 loss</p>
<p> Gross result		144.72 loss vs	   133.12 loss</p>
<p> Operating result	  124.62 loss vs	   114.40 loss</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services		561.13	vs	   747.46</p>
<p> Total assets	    5,921.48	vs	 6,852.54</p>
<p> Basic capital	   3,318.74	vs	 3,318.74</p>
<p>NOTE: Biocel is a leading pulp maker in the Czech Republic.</p>
<p>The Cyprus-based consortium Daventree of Bahamas-based investor Michael Dingman's Stratton Investments and Czech investment house Harvard Capital and Consulting hold a 33 percent stake in Biocel. Bankovni Holding a.s., an investment fund controlled by bank IPB a.s. holds an 11 percent stake.</p>
<p>Biocel shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange (PSE). Results were provided by the PSE.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
